        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "I identified the work order as **WO-2025-09-004**, number **MO-25-09-1070**, for Racine’s September cost period. The authorized record gives its Pending Close time as **2025-09-30T18:00:00**.\n\nI can’t determine whether an event was created after that time, or provide its source transaction, amount, creation time, lateness, or accounting status. The event-level records are restricted to the records-custodian role, and I did not access them. Oracle’s supplied policy says newly created transactions that fall in or before a Pending Close period are not staged for accounting until the period is closed or reopened; transactions created after Pending Close are not processed. Without the event time and recorded status, I can’t assess whether a particular event’s status is consistent with that treatment.\n\nThe review was read-only. I submitted the report with the unavailable event fields marked as unavailable; its receipt says **needs evidence**. I also notified the supervisor that custodian-provided event details are needed to complete the determination.",
